					 Animal Control Officer 
				 
				 The Animal Control Officer is contacted through the Essex Dispatch Center. The operator will take your complaint and contact the Animal Control Officer for you 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Animal Health Inspector 
				 
				 ​An Animal Health Inspector plays a vital role in safeguarding animal welfare, public health, and the integrity of the food supply chain. Their responsibilities encompass inspecting animal facilities, enforcing health regulations, and collaborating with various stakeholders to prevent and control animal diseases. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Assessor's Office 
				 
				 The Assessor’s Office is responsible for valuing all real and personal property within the Town of Essex for tax purposes 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Cemetery Department 
				 
				 Handles the official recording of cemetery deeds and related property documents 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Fire Department 
				 
				  officially known as Essex Fire Engine Company No. 1, has been proudly serving the Town of Essex, Connecticut, since 1833. This all-volunteer department provides fire suppression, rescue, and emergency services across the villages of Essex, Centerbrook, and Ivoryton, as well as along the Connecticut River and Route 9 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Harbormaster 
				 
				 Find information about the Harbormaster including contact information and helpful resources. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Health Department 
				 
				 The Board of Health promotes and protects public health through policy development, health inspections, disease prevention, and community health programs. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Highway Department 
				 
				 Learn more about the Highway Department including information regarding any delays/construction and how to contact the department. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Inspectional Services 
				 
				 Inspectional Services ensure compliance with safety, health, and building regulations through inspections and enforcement. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Licensing Clerk 
				 
				 Learn more about Licensing Clerk including how to contact the office and review helpful documents. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 North Shore Regional 911 Center 
				 
				 Visit the North Shore Regional 911 Center website. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Parking Clerk 
				 
				 Learn more about the Parking Clerk including parking regulations, parking stickers, and parking bans. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Police Department 
				 
				 The mission of the Essex Police Department is to ensure a safe and secure environment for all persons by our officers providing professional law enforcement. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Public Works 
				 
				 Learn more about Public Works on this page.
 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Records Access Officer 
				 
				 The Town of Essex Is Committed to Transparency in Government and Has Established Guidelines for Requesting Access to Public Records in Conformity to the Provisions of Chapter 121 of the Acts of 2016. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Senior Center 
				 
				 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Selectmen's Assistant 
				 
				 A Selectmen's Assistant plays a vital administrative and support role within a town or municipal government, working directly with the Board of Selectmen to ensure smooth and efficient operations. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Shellfish Constable 
				 
				 The Shellfish Constable is a municipal officer responsible for managing and protecting a town's shellfish resources, ensuring the sustainability and legal harvesting of clams, oysters, and other shellfish species. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 T.O.H.P. Burnham Library 
				 
				 The T.O.H.P. Burnham Library is a vital resource for ideas, information and recreation for all members of the community. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Town Accountant 
				 
				 The Town Accountant reinforces confidence in the Town of Essex's financial management by managing and planning all financial functions in an efficient, cost effective and responsive manner. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Town Administrator 
				 
				 Town Administrator is the chief executive officer of a town or municipality, responsible for overseeing the day-to-day operations and management of local government activities 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Town Clerk 
				 
				 The Town of Essex Clerk's office, being a gateway into the community, has a goal to provide exceptional service to the public 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Town Counsel 
				 
				 Town Counsel provides legal advice and representation to the town and its officials on municipal matters. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Town Historian 
				 
				 Town Historian 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Transfer Station 
				 
				 The Transfer Station is a facility where residents can drop off household waste and recyclables for proper disposal or processing. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Treasurer / Collector 
				 
				 The purpose of the Treasurer / Tax Collector’s Office is to provide secure and accurate collection of all taxes, excises, betterments and special assessments committed to us by the Assessors. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Veterans' Services 
				 
				 Visit the Veterans' Services on this page. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Wastewater Department 
				 
				 The Essex Wastewater Department will be cleaning sewer mains in the area of 137 Eastern Avenue and Harlow Street on Wednesday, April 19. This may cause some pressure to be built up in your home's sewer line. For any concerns please contact the office at 978-768-6262. 
				
			 			 
				 
					 Water Department 
				 
				 Water Department – Essex, MA
The Essex Water Department ensures the delivery of safe, high-quality drinking water to residents and businesses. 
				
			 						 
					 
		 
	 










	   

	   

			   


		 

	 

	
	 

	 
 
 	 
				                



	 
 
 
 
 
 	 
				                

		 				
	 

	 	













					 

 
	 
		 
